<title>UK: British Gas eases as bid hopes fade.</title>
<headline>British Gas eases as bid hopes fade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Gas fell on Tuesday amid talk Shell Transport ruled out a merger with with British Gas, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares, trimming the recent rally sustained on hopes for a takeover or merger, were down 4-1/2p to 231p at 1341 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;There doesn't seem to be anyone else in the frame at the moment,&quot; said one dealer.</p>
<p>No one at Shell was immediately available to comment.</p>
<p>Market speculation sparked an early flurry of trading in British Gas options. By 1341 GMT, more than 1,000 puts and about 250 calls changed hands.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
